                <pb facs="0741" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg727"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center"><seg type="margin">[741]</seg> *[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moore, collector of customs, to Mr. Boutwell,
                        Secretary of the Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House,
                            Philadelphia</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector’s
                        Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-04-08"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">April</hi> 8, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your letter of the 5th
                    instant, inclosing copy of letter from Secretary of State in relation to an
                    apprehended violation of the neutrality laws in fitting out steamer Florida at
                    Chester, Pennsylvania.</p>
                <p>I have fully advised the commanding officer of the revenue-steamer Seward what
                    course to pursue, and have also communicated with assistant surveyor at Chester
                    in relation to the matter, a copy of whose letter is herewith inclosed.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HENRY D. MOORE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector of
                        Customs.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. S. Boutwell</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasury, Washington, D.
                        C</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
